# Bonny Pall, Clearcutter: it enters in turn 3 and makes Beau, a legendary blue Ox whose power and toughness are the lands
# Bot1 controls (CR 604.3): 1/1 with one Island, Bot2's two Plains not counted. In turn 5 Bonny attacks (reach doesn't stop
# it attacking; it shows as a keyword); the trigger draws a card, then Bot1 puts the Forest Entomb binned in turn 1 from its
# graveyard onto the battlefield: Beau 2/2. That isn't a land play (2024-04-12 ruling): an Island drawn in turn 5 is
# still played after combat, Beau 3/3. Hand: Bonny after turn 1; the Island drawn and played, Bonny cast: 0; the turn-5
# draw and the trigger's card (Islands; Entomb shuffled the library) 2, one played 1.
# Bonny Pall, Clearcutter {3}{G}{U}{U}: Legendary Creature - Giant Scout 6/5
#   Reach
#   When Bonny Pall enters, create Beau, a legendary blue Ox creature token with "Beau's power and toughness are each
#   equal to the number of lands you control."
#   Whenever you attack, draw a card, then you may put a land card from your hand or graveyard onto the battlefield.

